    {
      "id": "b1-03",
      "title": "Pronoun position and shape",
      "goal": "Attach pronouns after infinitives, gerunds and imperatives.",
      "note": "Before a conjugated verb: full forms (**em, et, el...**). After an infinitive, gerund or imperative they hang on with a hyphen or apostrophe:\n\n- after a **vowel**: reduced → **mira'm**, **compra'l**, **escolta'ns**, **lleva't**\n- after a **consonant or -u**: full → **comprar-lo**, **conèixer-los**, **buscant-te**\n\nInfinitives in -re end in a vowel, so: **veure't**, **beure'l**, **treure-ho** (ho is always -ho).\n\nWith two verbs you can also put the pronoun first: **Et vull veure = Vull veure't**.",
      "tables": [
